  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Programm Stadtentwicklung/Abwasser</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wastewater Disposal and Solid Waste Management in Provincial Towns 2010</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Das FZ-Modulziel ist die Verbesserung der Abwasser- und Abfallentsorgung in den Provinzst&#xe4;dten entsprechend der wirtschaftlichen Leistungsf&#xe4;higkeit der Zielgruppe.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project is part of the Joint Development Cooperation (DC) Program Sustainable Urban Development: Municipal Environmental Management. It covers the expansion and rehabilitation of sewage networks and the construction of wastewater treatment plants in the provincial cities of Lang Son, Son La, and Hoa Binh Ninh in northern Vietnam. It also includes the second investment phase in Soc Trang. The aim is to improve urban wastewater and waste infrastructure in an economically, ecologically, and socially sustainable manner in order to enhance the quality of life of the population, especially in inner-city neighborhoods with neglected waste disposal infrastructure. The aim is to ensure that operating costs can be covered by fee revenues after completion. The Technical Cooperation (TC) module of the development cooperation program aims to improve the sectoral framework conditions, the performance of the program implementers, public awareness, and the monitoring of environmental impacts. Approximately 70% of the investment costs are to be financed from FC funds, with the remaining 30% coming from the Vietnamese side. The consulting costs will be financed by a grant from Switzerland (SECO) as a mandate. The target group is the population living in the program area, especially in inner-city neighborhoods with neglected waste disposal infrastructure, as well as those living downstream.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Das Projekt ist ein Teil des Gemeinsamen Entwicklungszusammenarbeit (EZ) Programms Nachhaltige Stadtentwicklung: Kommunales Umweltmanagement. Es umfasst den Ausbau und die Rehabilitierung der Abwassernetze und den Bau von Kl&#xe4;ranlagen in den Provinzst&#xe4;dten Lang Son, Son La und Hoa Binh Ninh im Norden Vietnams. Au&#xdf;erdem beinhaltet es die zweite Investitionsphase in Soc Trang. Ziel ist es, die urbane Abwasser- und Abfallinfrastruktur &#xf6;konomisch, &#xf6;kologisch und sozial nachhaltig zu verbessern, um die Lebensqualit&#xe4;t der Bev&#xf6;lkerung, insbesondere in innerst&#xe4;dtischen Vierteln mit vernachl&#xe4;ssigter Entsorgungsinfrastruktur, zu erh&#xf6;hen. Der Ma&#xdf;nahmenumfang der Teilvorhaben orientiert sich daran, dass die Betriebskosten nach Fertigstellung &#xfc;ber Geb&#xfc;hreneinnahmen gedeckt werden k&#xf6;nnen. Die sektoralen Rahmenbedingungen, die Leistungsf&#xe4;higkeit der Programmtr&#xe4;ger, die Sensibilisierung der Bev&#xf6;lkerung und die &#xdc;berwachung der Umweltwirkungen sollen durch das Technische Zusammenarbeit (TZ) Modul des EZ-Programms verbessert werden. Aus den FZ-Mitteln sollen rd. 70% der Investitionskosten finanziert werden, rd. 30% werden von vietnamesischer Seite finanziert. Die Consultingkosten werden aus einem Zuschuss der Schweiz (SECO) als Mandat finanziert. Zielgruppe des FZ-Moduls ist die im Programmgebiet lebende Bev&#xf6;lkerung, insbesondere in innerst&#xe4;dtischen Vierteln mit vernachl&#xe4;ssigter Entsorgungsinfrastruktur.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project is part of the Joint Development Cooperation (DC) Program Sustainable Urban Development: Municipal Environmental Management. It covers the expansion and rehabilitation of sewage networks and the construction of wastewater treatment plants in the provincial cities of Lang Son, Son La, and Hoa Binh Ninh in northern Vietnam. It also includes the second investment phase in Soc Trang. The aim is to improve urban wastewater and waste infrastructure in an economically, ecologically, and socially sustainable manner in order to enhance the quality of life of the population, especially in inner-city neighborhoods with neglected waste disposal infrastructure. The aim is to ensure that operating costs can be covered by fee revenues after completion. The Technical Cooperation (TC) module of the development cooperation program aims to improve the sectoral framework conditions, the performance of the program implementers, public awareness, and the monitoring of environmental impacts. Approximately 70% of the investment costs are to be financed from FC funds, with the remaining 30% coming from the Vietnamese side. The consulting costs will be financed by a grant from Switzerland (SECO) as a mandate. The target group is the population living in the program area, especially in inner-city neighborhoods with neglected waste disposal infrastructure, as well as those living downstream.</narrative>
  </description>
